Why doesn't this wait for the saves to finish?

```js
items.forEach(async (item) => {
  await save(item);
});
console.log("done");
```

forEach ignores the promises its callback returns, so "done" logs immediately. Use a for...of loop to save sequentially:

```js
for (const item of items) {
  await save(item);
}
```

or Promise.all to run them in parallel:

```js
await Promise.all(items.map(save));
```

